<title>SWITZERLAND: NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CUP COMBINED RESULTS.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CUP COMBINED RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST. MORITZ, Switzerland 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading official</p>
<p>results of a men's World Cup nordic combined event on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Mario Stecher (Austria) Total time 40 minutes, 48.8 seconds</p>
<p>(ski jumping 230.4 points/15km cross-country 40:48.8)</p>
<p>2. Bjarte Engen Vik (Norway) 41:00.8 (227.2/40:41.8) </p>
<p>3. Samppa Lajunen (Finland) 41:28.2 (204.4/38:52.2) </p>
<p>4. Hannu Manninen (Finland) 41:37.8 (206.5/39:14.8) </p>
<p>5. Knut Tore Apeland (Norway) 42:05.5 (208.1/39:51.5) </p>
<p>6. Todd Lodwick (U.S.) 42:18.2 (214.5/40:43.2) </p>
<p>7. Jari Mantila (Finland) 42:50.7 (206.2/40:25.7) </p>
<p>8. Valeri Stolyarov (Russia) 43:14.1 (214.8/41:40.1) </p>
<p>9. Fabrice Guy (France) 43:44.3 (187.1/39:24.3) </p>
<p>10. Tapio Nurmela (Finland) 44:07.4 (191.2/40:12.4)</p>
<p>World Cup standings:</p>
<p>1. Lajunen		    750 points</p>
